{
  "title": "Long vowel sounds",
  "kind": "phonics",
  "cefr": "A0",
  "estMinutes": 7,
  "intro": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Long sounds"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Vowels can also have a long sound. Two letters together often make one long sound."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": true,
      "rows": [
        [
          "letters",
          "word",
          "word"
        ],
        [
          "ee",
          "see",
          "sheep"
        ],
        [
          "ar",
          "car",
          "park"
        ],
        [
          "oo",
          "food",
          "school"
        ],
        [
          "or",
          "door",
          "four"
        ],
        [
          "ir",
          "bird",
          "girl"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Short or long?"
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "Pairs to listen for",
      "points": [
        "ship (short i) — sheep (long ee)",
        "full (short u) — fool (long oo)",
        "Long sounds are longer: sheeeep. Short sounds are quick: ship."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "Silent e",
      "points": [
        "An e at the end often makes the vowel say its name.",
        "cap → cape, kit → kite, hop → hope, cut → cute"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Grammar focus: plural -s"
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "One and more than one",
      "points": [
        "Most words add -s for more than one: one car, two cars; one bird, three birds.",
        "A few words do not change: one sheep, two sheep."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Be careful!"
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "two sheeps",
      "right": "two sheep",
      "why": "sheep does not change"
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "a ship eats grass",
      "right": "a sheep eats grass",
      "why": "ship = boat, sheep = animal"
    }
  ],
